#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# function_period

#% text
# `function_period(f, x)` gives the smallest positive period of `f` in `x`, and `0` when `f` is not periodic; `function_period(f, n, integers)` the period of a sequence; for several variables a list of periods, one per variable with the others fixed; over the complexes a list with one complex period.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Every periodic subterm `g(a x + b)` contributes the period of `g` divided by `a` (`2 pi` for `sin`, `pi` for `tan`, `2 pi im` for `exp` and `cosh`, `m` for `mod(u, m)`); powers `c^(a x)` of constants are exponentials (`(-1)^n` has the period 2).

#% item
# The candidates must have rational ratios; their least common multiple `T` is a period, and the smallest one is the largest `T/k` (`k <= 24`) that checks numerically at six points to 30 digits. Over the integers the period is the smallest divisor of the integer period that checks.

#% item
# Over the reals a period that is not real, a polynomial or incommensurable periods mean no period: `0`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
function_period(sin(x), x)
#% output
#= 2*pi

#% cell
function_period(mod(n, 8), n, integers)
#% output
#= 8

#% cell
function_period(cos(x) + sin(y), [x, y])
#% output
#= [2*pi, 2*pi]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Sequences:

#% cell
[function_period((-1)^n, n, integers), function_period(sin(2*pi*n/17 + 3), n, integers), function_period(mod(2*n, 18), n, integers)]
#% output
#= [2, 17, 9]

#% cell
function_period(mod(n^3 + 7*n^2 + 3, 11), n, integers)
#% output
#= 11

#% text
# A root of unity:

#% cell
function_period(exp(2*pi*im*n/7), n, integers)
#% output
#= 7

#% text
# Complex periods:

#% cell
[function_period(exp(z), z, complexes), function_period(cosh(z), z, complexes)]
#% output
#= [[2im*pi], [2im*pi]]

#% text
# A parameter under an assumption:

#% cell
assuming(a > 0, function_period(sin(a*x), x))
#% output
#= 2*pi/a

#% text
# Several variables:

#% cell
function_period([tan(x + y), cos(x - 2*y)], [x, y])
#% output
#= [2*pi, pi]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A square halves the period:

#% cell
function_period(sin(x)^2, x)
#% output
#= pi

#% text
# Not periodic:

#% cell
[function_period(x^2, x), function_period(sin(x) + sin(sqrt(2)*x), x), function_period(exp(x), x)]
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0]

#% text
# The period reproduces the values (the difference at a sample point is at rounding level):

#% cell
f = sin(3*x) + cos(x/2)
T = function_period(f, x)
[T, abs((f /. x -> 0.4) - (f /. x -> 0.4 + n(T))) < 10^-12]
#% output
#= [4*pi, true]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# `x - floor(x)` has the period 1; a constant function has no smallest period and gives 0; an undefined function stays unevaluated:

#% cell
[function_period(x - floor(x), x), function_period(1, x), function_period(g(x), x)]
#% output
#= [1, 0, function_period(g(x), x)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `function_poles`, `function_domain`, `mod`
